common_mistakes.tern:9:5: error: cannot assign to input port `a`
  |
9 |     a = 3
  |     ^^^^^
  = help: inputs are driven by the instantiating module; for a value computed here use an `out` port or a `let`/`var`
  in: AssignInput

common_mistakes.tern:16:5: error: cannot assign to input port `s.valid`
   |
16 |     s.valid = true
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: `s.valid` flows into this module: on an `in` bundle port only the `flip` fields are outputs
  in: AssignBundleInput

common_mistakes.tern:26:12: error: register `r` can only be assigned in an `on` block
   |
26 |     comb { r = a }
   |            ^^^^^
   = help: a `comb` block assigns `var`s and outputs: declare `var r: ...` for a combinational value, or assign the register in `on`
  in: RegInComb

common_mistakes.tern:34:5: error: cannot assign to `t`: a `let` is assigned once, at its declaration
   |
34 |     t = a +% 1
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: for a value assigned in a block, declare `var t: ...` (comb) or `reg t: ...` (on)
  in: LetReassign

common_mistakes.tern:47:21: error: module `Child` has no port `b`
   |
47 |     y = Child(a: a, b: a).y
   |                     ^
   = help: its ports are `a`, `y`
  in: UnknownPort

common_mistakes.tern:54:11: error: module `Child` has no port `yy`
   |
54 |     y = c.yy
   |           ^^
   = help: its ports are `a`, `y`
  in: MisspelledPort

common_mistakes.tern:60:16: error: enum `Op` has no variant `Ad`
   |
60 |     y = op == .Ad
   |                ^^
   = help: did you mean `.Add`?
  in: EnumTypo

common_mistakes.tern:67:9: error: cannot compare uint<8> with bool
   |
67 |     y = a == b
   |         ^^^^^^
   = help: convert the bool with `b as uint<1>`, or test the integer with `x != 0`
  in: CompareBool

common_mistakes.tern:74:9: error: an `if` used as a value needs an `else`
   |
74 |     y = if c { a }
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^
   = help: add `else { ... }` with a value of the same type
  in: IfWithoutElse

common_mistakes.tern:82:17: error: the reset value of `r` must be a compile-time constant
   |
82 |     reg r: u8 = a
   |                 ^
   = help: a reset value is a constant; to load a signal, assign it in the `on` block
  in: ResetNotConstant

common_mistakes.tern:91:12: error: register `r` cannot hold a bundle (Valid<uint<8>>)
   |
91 |     reg r: Valid<u8>
   |            ^^^^^^^^^
   = help: declare one register per field (`reg r_valid: bool`), or use a struct type
  in: RegBundle

common_mistakes.tern:110:9: error: instance `clocked_0` of `Clocked` has unconnected input `clk`
    |
110 |     y = Clocked(a: a).y
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    = help: clock and reset ports are inherited only from a default domain (a module with one clock); connect `clk: ...` or put the instance in a domain: `Clocked(..) @ dom`
  in: TwoClocks

common_mistakes.tern:116:36: error: cannot find `missing` in this scope
    |
116 |     y = Valid { valid: true, data: missing }
    |                                    ^^^^^^^
  in: LiteralCascade

common_mistakes.tern:125:44: error: width mismatch: `c + 1` is uint<5>, expected uint<4>
    |
125 |         if en { c = if c == 9 { 0 } else { c + 1 } }
    |                                            ^^^^^
    = help: use `+%` for a wrapping add, or truncate with `as uint<4>`
  in: IfArmWidth

common_mistakes.tern:136:17: error: width mismatch: `a + b` is uint<9>, expected uint<8>
    |
136 |         .Add => a + b,
    |                 ^^^^^
    = help: use `+%` for a wrapping add, or truncate with `as uint<8>`
  in: MatchArmWidth

